# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Ablation caches ARE TRACKED as of 2026-09-05. They were ignored as
# "regenerable, and large" — the first is true and the second was not: all
# EIGHT together are 296 KB. Tracking them lets a clone reproduce or extend the
# tables without the run. The cost is that a stale cache can now arrive with a
# checkout, so ABLATION_CACHES.md records a source fingerprint per deck; check
# it before resuming one. See cache_manifest.py.
#
# TWELVE, not four, since 2026-09-06: each deck has the current N=15000
# `_medblank` cache, the N=15000 one it superseded the same day (measured
# against the old blank — see KNOWN_ISSUES.md 0j), and the N=6000 (tivit:
# N=2000) one before that. The older two are kept because they are the
# provenance for every number quoted in CLAUDE.md above their dates. The
# "roughly six hours to rebuild" that justified tracking them is no longer true
# either — the whole set is 23 minutes now. They stay tracked for provenance
# rather than for the compute.
#
# The blank mode is IN THE FILENAME on purpose: a cache measured against a
# different blank is not resumable onto, and a suffix nothing reads is how the
# N-in-the-key bug happened the first time.

# Spreadsheet lock/temp files
~$*.xlsx
.~lock.*

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Everything below moved under results/ in the 2026-09-09 reorganisation. The
# patterns are anchored there rather than left bare, so a stray ablation_*.log
# written into the root by a script run the wrong way is VISIBLE in git status
# instead of silently ignored.

# Ablation stderr progress logs — noise, the .txt tables are the artefact
results/ablation_*.log

# Regeneration scratch — the finished .txt tables ARE tracked
results/ablation_*.txt.new
results/regen.log

# A void table kept only long enough to diff against; not an artefact.
results/ablation_*_VOID_*.txt

# tutor_policy.py's scratch log
results/tutor_log.json

# check_unchanged_decks.py's baseline dumps
results/baselines*.json
